# 🌱 EcoPoints Recycling Tracker

A Java-based console application designed to manage household recycling activities, calculate eco-points based on material weights, persist records using binary serialization, and generate community-wide recycling reports.

---

## 🚀 Features

- **Household Management**: Register new households with unique IDs, names, addresses, and automatic join-date timestamps.
- **Recycling Event Logging**: Log drop-offs for various materials (plastic, glass, metal, paper) and automatically award eco-points.
- **Data Persistence**: Automatically saves and loads all system data using Java Object Serialization (`HouseholdData.ser`).
- **Detailed History & Reports**: View individual household recycling histories, total points, total community weight recycled, and identify the top recycler.
- **Robust Error Handling**: Handles invalid inputs, incorrect file paths, and unexpected formatting errors gracefully.

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

- **Language**: Java
- **Concepts**: Object-Oriented Programming (OOP), Collections Framework (`HashMap`, `ArrayList`), File I/O & Serialization, Exception Handling
- **Environment**: Java Development Kit (JDK), Visual Studio Code, Windows Terminal / PowerShell

---

## 📂 Project Structure

```text
EcoPoints_Recycling_Tracker/
│
└── src/
    ├── Household.java          # Household data model & point calculations
    ├── RecyclingEvent.java     # Recycling transaction model & point conversion logic
    ├── RecyclingManager.java   # Core business logic, HashMap storage, & file persistence
    ├── Main.java               # CLI interactive menu & exception handling
    └── HouseholdData.ser       # Generated binary storage file (created upon saving)